Hi.

I've a recurring problem w/ kernel 2.6.35.x that I cannot pinpoint exactly =
but
seems to be related to rcu_preempt_state stall warnings I get frequently.

=46rom time to time, the machine slows down to an almost halt (meaning jump=
y or
non-responsive mouse cursor, unable to switch to text console, ...) which c=
an
also result in a complete hang w/o any way to recover.   Sometimes the syst=
em
catches up again but once this happened,  the system is sluggish and a rebo=
ot
is required nevertheless. High load seems to help a lot to trigger this iss=
ue.

In every instance, I found stall warnings in my log which might be related.=
 I
have attached three of them along with my config and dmesg.

The system works flawlessly with pre-2.6.35 kernels-  no stall warnings and=
 no
slow-downs at all.

If there is anything I can do to help further diagnose this problem, please=
 let
me know.

So long,
matthias.

PS. Please cc' me because I am not subscribed to the list. Thanks a lot.

